1. INTRODUCTION

CHATORA is a Python-based Restaurant Management System designed to simplify and automate day-to-day restaurant operations such as staff registration, food ordering, billing, and table booking.

This system demonstrates the use of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) principles, modular design, and file-based JSON data storage, providing a lightweight yet functional restaurant management solution.

The project was developed as part of an internship under Mr. Kailash Singh Shahi (IndiXpert), during the Full Stack Web Development (One-Year Course), showcasing core concepts of software development and backend logic design.

2. OBJECTIVES

To design a modular and reusable Python package for managing restaurant operations.

To implement user authentication for admin and staff with secure data handling.

To enable menu management, order processing, and billing automation.

To support customer table booking for up to 20 tables.

To maintain persistent data using JSON files as a lightweight database alternative.

To demonstrate proper exception handling, input validation, and logging.

To apply Object-Oriented Programming principles for better maintainability and scalability.

3. SYSTEM OVERVIEW

The system is structured into modular components within the package:
restaurant_management_system/

1. authentication/

Handles user management and security functions.

registration.py → Provides functionality for admin and staff signin/signup.

2. domain/

Manages the core business logic.

menu_order.py → Handles menu creation, food ordering, billing, and table management.

validation.py → Defines a Validation class for input checks (e.g., mobile numbers, email formats, etc.).

logs.py → Logs key activities and operations into logs.json.

table_booking.py → Reserved for future extension of the table booking system.

3. database/

Contains persistent data files in JSON format for lightweight database simulation.

staff.json – Stores staff details and credentials.

menu.json – Stores available food items and prices.

orders.json – Stores all customer orders and billing details.

bookings.json – Records table bookings and related data.

logs.json – Logs all system activities for audit and debugging purposes.

4. main.py

Acts as the entry point of the system.
Provides a console-based menu with options for:

Signin

Signup (Admin only)

Exit

4. FEATURES AND FUNCTIONALITY

Admin Module

Add, view, and manage staff accounts.

Create and update menu items.

Staff Module

Sign in and take customer orders.

Generate and print customer bills.

Book tables for customers.

Data Persistence

All data (staff, menu, orders, etc.) are stored and managed through JSON files.

Validation & Logging

Ensures proper user inputs and maintains system logs for each operation.

